/// If multiple are set then the `storage_connection_string` is given priority.
///
/// If the `storage_connection_string` does not contain the `AccountName` parameter,
/// please specify it in the
/// `storage_account` field.
///
/// ## Tags
///
/// The `tags` field allows you to attach key/value pairs to blobs as [blob index
/// tags](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-manage-find-blobs),
/// where the values support [interpolation
/// functions](https://docs.redpanda.com/redpanda-connect/configuration/interpolation#bloblang-queries):
///
/// ```yaml
/// output:
///   azure_blob_storage:
///     container: TODO
///     path: ${!counter()}-${!timestamp_unix_nano()}.txt
///     tags:
///       Environment: production
///       Source: ${!@kafka_topic}
/// ```
///
/// Keys and values can contain only alphanumerics, spaces, and the characters `+ - . / :
/// = _`. Only values support interpolation. Keys are static and are checked against
/// Azure's limits at startup. Values are resolved and checked per message, and a message
/// with an invalid value fails before any upload.
///
/// If authenticating with `storage_sas_token`, the token must include the `t` (tags)
/// permission.
///
/// When `blob_type` is `APPEND` the tags describe the blob rather than any single
/// message, so they are applied only when this output creates the blob, and are not
/// re-sent with subsequent appends. Two consequences are worth knowing:
///
